profile: minimodel.totem.current.v1
updated_utc: 2026-08-28T00:00:00Z
site: MiniModel.org
role: positive operating authority
authority_file_mutability: read_only_without_exact_human_artifact_and_operation_authorization

site_authority:
  - MiniModel.org is the bounded metadata catalog and direct-P2P discovery surface for qualified SLM2 compositions.
  - It does not proxy model bytes. Exact qualified bytes move directly between consenting peers or are converted explicitly by an installed local companion.
  - The owner authorizes MiniModel.org to provide the initial verified current SLM2 seeds from D:\LLMs\TinyRustLM. TinyRustLM restores a usable cached model or automatically acquires a small qualified starter; Hugging Face, local files, conversion, and manual peer/IP settings belong in Advanced.
  - Hosting authorization and source implementation do not prove a working qualified model, deployed seed service, or live public transfer.
  - Bind source, license, composition, profile, member, piece, qualification, runtime, and expiring peer identities cryptographically.
  - Keep catalog metadata, peer transfer, local execution, browser activation, and publication as separate claims.

clean_slate:
  - Use one current SLM2 catalog and acquisition contract with no legacy format, alias-to-different-bytes, hidden route retry, or remote-inference fallback.
  - Update implementation, documentation, examples, schemas, tests, and release records together, then remove superseded active paths.
  - Preserve immutable historical evidence without keeping obsolete production readers.

memory_endpoints_two_lane_authority:
  - MemoryEndpoints.com has exactly two distinct authorized uses across the ecosystem.
  - Agents working on all ecosystem sites use MemoryEndpoints.com directly for agent-to-agent long-term memory, meetings, handoffs, and coordination.
  - Separately, the TinyRustLM.com Connect plugin lets a user sign in to MemoryEndpoints.com and explicitly select it as TinyRustLM.com Connect long-term memory.
  - Keep lane identity, credentials, consent, scopes, provenance, idempotency, and receipts separate. MemoryEndpoints.com is not a model-byte transport, peer relay, catalog authority, or inference service.
  - Configuration and reachability do not prove live memory, account correctness, synchronization, restore, deletion, cleanup, continuity, or peer availability.

prelaunch_redundancy:
  - Important memory may also be kept in current .uai, wiki, public-safe source notes, and approved private stores for resilience.
  - Keep every maintained copy current, secret-safe, provenance-labeled, and noncontradictory.
  - Surface and reconcile conflicts; do not silently choose one contradictory copy.
